# EXPECT-VIOLATION: mirash:AssetClassInstanceShape
#
# Direction error: an installed drive is declared instance_of ANOTHER installed drive.
#
# This is the case InstanceOfDirectionShape was written for, and that shape does NOT fire here. The
# validator runs with RDFS inference and mira:instance_of declares rdfs:range mira:AssetClass, so
# the object is inferred to be an AssetClass before any shape looks at it; the direction check then
# always passes. What does fire is AssetClassInstanceShape, because vfd_102 now reads as both a
# model and an installed thing. So the mistake is rejected, by the neighbouring rule.
#
# InstanceOfDirectionShape is therefore listed in ../coverage-exclusions.json, and
# tests/test_ontology_coverage_gate.py pins the part that is NOT rejected (instance_of pointing at
# something that is not an asset at all).

@prefix mira: <https://ontology.factorylm.com/mira#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/fx#> .

ex:vfd_101 a mira:AssetInstance ; mira:instance_of ex:vfd_102 .
ex:vfd_102 a mira:AssetInstance .
